From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 23:33:35 +0200
Subject: wifi: mac80211: Fall back to mandatory rates if rate set matches no
 rate

Since commit 16ee3ea8faef ("wifi: mac80211: check basic rates validity
in sta_link_apply_parameters"), NL80211_CMD_NEW_STATION and
NL80211_CMD_SET_STATION fail with -EINVAL when none of the supplied
supported rates match the band of the interface.

This broke association of misbehaving-but-real stations. Some clients
(observed with a MediaTek-based device) send an association request on
5 GHz whose Supported Rates element contains only 11b rates
(1/2/5.5/11 Mbps) and no Extended Supported Rates element, even though
the same frame carries valid HT/VHT capabilities. hostapd passes the
rate set through to SET_STATION when marking the station associated,
mac80211 now rejects it, and hostapd fails the association with status
17 (AP_UNABLE_TO_HANDLE_NEW_STA). It gets worse from there: hostapd
caches the offending rates in its station entry and includes them in
the NEW_STATION it issues on the client's next authentication attempt
(ap_sta_re_add()), so even authentication keeps failing until the
station entry times out, after which the whole cycle repeats. The
client can never connect. Before the commit above, the unparseable
rates were simply ignored and such clients associated fine, exchanging
data over HT/VHT MCS rates.

Keep the protection against an empty rate bitmap (the original
commit's concern, found by syzkaller), but instead of rejecting the
station, fall back to the band's mandatory rates - the same fallback
IBSS and OCB already use. Any station transmitting on a band must
support that band's mandatory rates per 802.11, so this is a safe
minimal assumption, and legacy rates are irrelevant for HT/VHT-capable
stations anyway.

Fixes: 16ee3ea8faef ("wifi: mac80211: check basic rates validity in sta_link_apply_parameters")
Signed-of-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 net/mac80211/cfg.c | 14 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/cfg.c b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/cfg.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
@@ -2181,8 +2181,18 @@ static int sta_link_apply_parameters(struct ieee80211_local *local,
 	    params->supported_rates_len &&
 	    !ieee80211_parse_bitrates(sband, params->supported_rates,
 				      params->supported_rates_len,
-				      &link_sta->pub->supp_rates[sband->band]))
-		return -EINVAL;
+				      &link_sta->pub->supp_rates[sband->band])) {
+		/*
+		 * Some misbehaving stations report legacy rates of the
+		 * wrong band in their (re)association request (e.g. 11b
+		 * rates on 5 GHz), so none of them may parse. Rejecting
+		 * the station outright would prevent it from ever
+		 * associating; fall back to the band's mandatory rates
+		 * instead, which also keeps the rate bitmap non-empty.
+		 */
+		link_sta->pub->supp_rates[sband->band] =
+			ieee80211_mandatory_rates(sband);
+	}
 
 	if (params->ht_capa)
 		ieee80211_ht_cap_ie_to_sta_ht_cap(sdata, own_ht_cap,
-- 
